WEBVTT

00:06:30.083 --> 00:06:32.184
The range allows you
to signal a bottom line

00:06:32.208 --> 00:06:34.268
without having to disclose one,

00:06:34.292 --> 00:06:38.684
and it makes you look more flexible
than if you anchor with a single number.

00:06:38.708 --> 00:06:42.309
People are concerned about insulting you
by going below your range,

00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:44.500
so they're more likely
to counter within it.

00:06:45.625 --> 00:06:49.059
You can take this a step further
if you're negotiating multiple issues.

00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:51.643
Put multiple offers on the table.

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:53.351
This might sound counterintuitive

00:06:53.375 --> 00:06:55.934
if you're used to sticking
with a single set of terms,

00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:58.059
but research shows
you're better off working

00:06:58.083 --> 00:07:00.934
from what's called a multiple
equivalent simultaneous offer.